  "plain": "In 2023, a whistleblower named David Grusch came forward to the US government. A guest named Merrick von Rennenkampf says Grusch had people with firsthand knowledge go to the inspector general, an internal government watchdog, to file a complaint, and that, in his telling, a man named Lou Elizondo said under oath that the US has programmes to recover crashed craft. A podcast host, Jesse Michels, says Grusch brought 40 firsthand whistleblowers to the inspector general for the intelligence agencies, Thomas Monheim, who called the claims urgent and credible. If true, it would mean the US government secretly holds craft that are not of human making."
